from pages10 import notice
PAGES=[
notice('facebook-your-account-has-been-disabled-notice','Facebook','Your account has been disabled','“Your Account Has Been Disabled” on Facebook: What to Do (2026)','Facebook disabled the profile for a rule it names, or for not following its terms. If a “Disagree with decision” or review option shows, the decision can still be reviewed. If no option shows, the review window may have closed.','<strong>“Your account has been disabled” on Facebook means the profile is off, but a review option may still be open.</strong> Look for a disagree or review button on the notice and use it once, in plain words. Do not create a new profile while you wait. Meta makes the final decision.',['Screenshot the notice and note the date.','Look for a review or disagree option and use it once.','Check that your email and phone on file still work.','Do not open a new profile while waiting.'],[('Can a disabled Facebook profile come back?','Sometimes, if a review is still open and Meta agrees. Nobody can promise an outcome.'),('There is no review button. What now?','See the no-appeal-button guide and the official links directory.')]),
notice('facebook-your-account-has-been-locked-notice','Facebook','Your account has been locked','“Your Account Has Been Locked” on Facebook: What It Means (2026)','A lock is usually a security step, not a ban. Facebook saw unusual activity, such as a login from a new place, and wants you to confirm it is you before you continue.','<strong>“Your account has been locked” on Facebook is usually a security check, not a disabled account.</strong> Click the get-started option, follow the steps on the device you normally use, and change your password once you are back in. Meta makes the final decision.',['Use the device and network you normally use.','Follow the on-screen steps to confirm it is you.','Change your password and turn on two-factor authentication once inside.','Check recent logins and remove devices you do not recognise.'],[('Is a locked account the same as disabled?','No. A lock asks you to confirm your identity. A disabled account was turned off for a rule.'),('The unlock steps keep failing. What now?','Wait before retrying, then try from your usual device. See the official links directory.')]),
notice('facebook-we-received-your-information-notice','Facebook','We received your information','“We Received Your Information” on Facebook: What It Means (2026)','This message confirms Facebook got your appeal or ID. It does not mean a decision was made. Reviews can take a varying amount of time, and Facebook does not share a set timeline.','<strong>“We received your information” means your appeal or ID arrived, not that it was approved.</strong> Do not send the same appeal again and again. Keep the confirmation, watch your email and the Support Inbox, and wait for the decision. Meta makes the final decision.',['Screenshot the confirmation and note the date.','Do not resubmit the same form repeatedly.','Watch your email and the Support Inbox.','Do not open a new account while waiting.'],[('Should I send the form again?','Usually not. Repeat submissions do not speed things up.'),('How long does it take?','Meta does not share a set timeline, and it varies.')]),
notice('instagram-we-received-your-appeal-notice','Instagram','We received your appeal','“We Received Your Appeal” on Instagram: What It Means (2026)','Instagram confirms the appeal arrived and is waiting for a decision. It does not mean the account will be restored. Instagram does not give a set timeline.','<strong>“We received your appeal” means Instagram has your request, not that it was approved.</strong> Avoid sending more appeals for the same account. Keep the confirmation email, check that it came from an @mail.instagram.com address, and wait. Instagram makes the final decision.',['Screenshot the confirmation.','Check the sender is @mail.instagram.com.','Do not appeal again for the same decision.','Ignore messages from people offering paid restores in DMs.'],[('Does this mean my account is coming back?','No. It only confirms the appeal arrived.'),('Someone DMed offering to speed it up. Is that real?','Treat it as a scam. Instagram does not sell faster reviews.')]),
notice('instagram-your-account-is-under-review-notice','Instagram','Your account is under review','“Your Account Is Under Review” on Instagram: What It Means (2026)','Instagram is checking the account after an appeal, an ID or a video selfie. During this time you usually cannot use the account. There is no set timeline.','<strong>“Your account is under review” means Instagram is deciding, so the best step is usually to wait.</strong> Do not create new accounts or send extra appeals. Keep your email and phone reachable. Instagram makes the final decision.',['Screenshot the notice and date.','Keep your email and phone reachable.','Do not open new accounts while waiting.','Do not send extra appeals for the same decision.'],[('Can I speed up the review?','No reliable way exists. Repeat appeals do not help.'),('What if it says under review for weeks?','It varies. See the official links directory for the right form.')]),
]
